{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954670-k9ine-s-homebrew","id":954670,"title":"K9ine's Homebrew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-20T16:03:00-07:00","id":954670,"title":"K9ine's Homebrew","content":"I am still very new to CofD in general, so some of these things might not be balanced as well as they should, but I thought they were fun. Feel free to take a look. So far I have made a merit that gives the Nosferatu the body horror that it is implied they sometimes possess. There is also a discipline that reflects the research of a Mekhet occultist.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ALOiJFwAzBVS8XAVXmQygLm5M1XV2vIXUK9Yx8bbfzI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ALOiJFwAzBVS8XAVXmQygLm5M1XV2vIXUK9Yx8bbfzI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ALOiJFwAzBVS8XAVXmQygLm5M1XV2vIXUK9Yx8bbfzI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ALOiJFwAzBVS8XAVXmQygLm5M1XV2vIXUK9Yx8bbfzI/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T16:42:59-07:00","id":954679,"title":"","content":"The merit is cheaper than buying Protean to two dots in clan which is where I'd look for such a power (honestly it could be 4 dots) and you should check out the Khaibit in the Bloodlines and stuff sticky for something like your discipline idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T16:58:03-07:00","id":954686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954670-k9ine-s-homebrew?p=954679#post954679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The merit is cheaper than buying Protean to two dots in clan which is where I'd look for such a power (honestly it could be 4 dots) and you should check out the Khaibit in the Bloodlines and stuff sticky for something like your discipline idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean my merit is too expensive or too cheap? Sorry i'm confused because you said that its cheap but could be four dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T17:31:24-07:00","id":954693,"title":"","content":"I think it was mentioned before, but you should take a look at Holger: The Butcher Worm from Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners. I feel like they are in a similar path; both Nos that no longer be considered human. (yes I know that from a distance your Nos is suppose to look relatively normal. But I feel that the stronger he gets, the less he does). There is an incredibly powerful devotion in there if you don't mind not being able to interact with humans. Although the main downside is that it reduces your speed.. Although I'm sure there could be something to bypass that. I think you could come up with something absolutely terrifying with that. <br /> <br /> Do note though, that you have to be fairly old to use the devotion (I think it's a minimum of BP 5, plus a lot of disciplines around 4).<br /> <br /> Edit: There is actually a second devotion from Holger that gives him a ridiculously strong bite attack. Might be a goal you want for your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","user":"Krzyzstof","date":". 08-20-2016, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T17:33:53-07:00","id":954699,"title":"","content":"I mean that it feels like it is comparable in power to the 4th dot in Protean (admirably it would be free to use after paying to activate it rather than paying each time you use it) but having opened the book and read what goes where I'm rethinking that as it's less powerful than flight.<br /> Given that the merit is better than Wall Climbing I don't think it's appropriate as a single Predatory Aspect but I would approach this as a job for Protean rather than trying to make a merit.<br /> I've just read the other thread you've got about this and my advice for what it's worth is 1 see if your ST will let you start as a Bloodline such as the Noctuku (There's even stuff in there lore about people spontaneously joining) and starting with as many dots in Protean as you can and 2 ignore RAW if you ST is ok with you doing it, yes they're right about the rules but no one cares.<br /> Assuming this is still for the Strix embraced game unless the ST has a reason he doesn't want it to happen it's his call what you can be (Maybe the Strix had a Noctuku body when he made you.<br /> Above all else have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T17:42:52-07:00","id":954705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954670-k9ine-s-homebrew?p=954699#post954699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that it feels like it is comparable in power to the 4th dot in Protean (admirably it would be free to use after paying to activate it rather than paying each time you use it) but having opened the book and read what goes where I'm rethinking that as it's less powerful than flight.<br /> Given that the merit is better than Wall Climbing I don't think it's appropriate as a single Predatory Aspect but I would approach this as a job for Protean rather than trying to make a merit.<br /> I've just read the other thread you've got about this and my advice for what it's worth is 1 see if your ST will let you start as a Bloodline such as the Noctuku (There's even stuff in there lore about people spontaneously joining) and starting with as many dots in Protean as you can and 2 ignore RAW if you ST is ok with you doing it, yes they're right about the rules but no one cares.<br /> Assuming this is still for the Strix embraced game unless the ST has a reason he doesn't want it to happen it's his call what you can be (Maybe the Strix had a Noctuku body when he made you.<br /> Above all else have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I come from the school of thought that if their is a power in a book, you should customize it to make it fit your character. This is why I made it a merit, instead of a devotion, or other bloodline power. I grew up watching anime, where characters may have many of the same abilities, but they find unique ways to use them. I do have that bloodlines book with the Noctuku, but it dosent seem to relatet to my character idea. I'm not really sure its Strix game though just speculation, my Storyteller just didn't want us to have sires because he said it would make transitioning to a vampire to easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-20-2016, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T17:45:34-07:00","id":954707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954670-k9ine-s-homebrew?p=954699#post954699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that it feels like it is comparable in power to the 4th dot in Protean (admirably it would be free to use after paying to activate it rather than paying each time you use it) but having opened the book and read what goes where I'm rethinking that as it's less powerful than flight.<br /> Given that the merit is better than Wall Climbing I don't think it's appropriate as a single Predatory Aspect but I would approach this as a job for Protean rather than trying to make a merit.<br /> I've just read the other thread you've got about this and my advice for what it's worth is 1 see if your ST will let you start as a Bloodline such as the Noctuku (There's even stuff in there lore about people spontaneously joining) and starting with as many dots in Protean as you can and 2 ignore RAW if you ST is ok with you doing it, yes they're right about the rules but no one cares.<br /> Assuming this is still for the Strix embraced game unless the ST has a reason he doesn't want it to happen it's his call what you can be (Maybe the Strix had a Noctuku body when he made you.<br /> Above all else have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I bought the wrong bloodline book unfortiantly, and I just started a new job and will be behind on rent next month, but i'm sure i'll check it out someday, although I don't know that I'll play vampire again. I want to get to HtV, BtP, CtL, WtF, and DnD 5th edition. Lot of games out there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:36:37-07:00","id":954824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954670-k9ine-s-homebrew?p=954699#post954699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that it feels like it is comparable in power to the 4th dot in Protean (admirably it would be free to use after paying to activate it rather than paying each time you use it) but having opened the book and read what goes where I'm rethinking that as it's less powerful than flight.<br /> Given that the merit is better than Wall Climbing I don't think it's appropriate as a single Predatory Aspect but I would approach this as a job for Protean rather than trying to make a merit.<br /> I've just read the other thread you've got about this and my advice for what it's worth is 1 see if your ST will let you start as a Bloodline such as the Noctuku (There's even stuff in there lore about people spontaneously joining) and starting with as many dots in Protean as you can and 2 ignore RAW if you ST is ok with you doing it, yes they're right about the rules but no one cares.<br /> Assuming this is still for the Strix embraced game unless the ST has a reason he doesn't want it to happen it's his call what you can be (Maybe the Strix had a Noctuku body when he made you.<br /> Above all else have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>He has been told about these being better fitting to protean and also the Nocktu bloodline. <br /> <br /> I love making unique fun homebrew stuff, but I don't think it's right to take way more powerful disciplines and make it a cheaper merit. It sort of screws over everyone else. If you make a merit that only costs 5 exp but it would cost a Gangrel with protean 6-12 exp. It doesn't seem fair, balanced or right. Or if you weren't a Gangrel and had to spend 8-16exp. <br /> <br /> I also wouldn't start making up stuff to change the game until you understand what you're changing. Don't make merits devotions and disciplines until you are fully aware of what is out there to make it fair and balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:54:30-07:00","id":954834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954670-k9ine-s-homebrew?p=954824#post954824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He has been told about these being better fitting to protean and also the Nocktu bloodline. <br /> <br /> I love making unique fun homebrew stuff, but I don't think it's right to take way more powerful disciplines and make it a cheaper merit. It sort of screws over everyone else. If you make a merit that only costs 5 exp but it would cost a Gangrel with protean 6-12 exp. It doesn't seem fair, balanced or right. Or if you weren't a Gangrel and had to spend 8-16exp. <br /> <br /> I also wouldn't start making up stuff to change the game until you understand what you're changing. Don't make merits devotions and disciplines until you are fully aware of what is out there to make it fair and balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, although granted if everyone is okay with it then let them be. But I do feel that if anything, it should be a devotion. Think it was mentioned earlier as something like Protean 2 (at least, although 4 does make more sense), Nightmare 1, Vigor 1. I would be inclined to offer two different versions. Maybe start with Protean 2 and Vigor 1 (like he originally wanted), and he is able to use them like tails/tentacles/whatever, but unable to feed until he gets the Protean 4 version. I like the idea of monsters growing, kind of like the aforementioned Holger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:58:07-07:00","id":954838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954670-k9ine-s-homebrew?p=954834#post954834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with this, although granted if everyone is okay with it then let them be. But I do feel that if anything, it should be a devotion. Think it was mentioned earlier as something like Protean 2 (at least, although 4 does make more sense), Nightmare 1, Vigor 1. I would be inclined to offer two different versions. Maybe start with Protean 2 and Vigor 1 (like he originally wanted), and he is able to use them like tails/tentacles/whatever, but unable to feed until he gets the Protean 4 version. I like the idea of monsters growing, kind of like the aforementioned Holger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes a few mentioned protean 2-4 + vigor devotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T23:01:34-07:00","id":954841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954670-k9ine-s-homebrew?p=954824#post954824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He has been told about these being better fitting to protean and also the Nocktu bloodline.<br /> <br /> I love making unique fun homebrew stuff, but I don't think it's right to take way more powerful disciplines and make it a cheaper merit. It sort of screws over everyone else. If you make a merit that only costs 5 exp but it would cost a Gangrel with protean 6-12 exp. It doesn't seem fair, balanced or right. Or if you weren't a Gangrel and had to spend 8-16exp.<br /> <br /> I also wouldn't start making up stuff to change the game until you understand what you're changing. Don't make merits devotions and disciplines until you are fully aware of what is out there to make it fair and balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just do it for fun. I don't expect to use the Mekhet thing, but I figure someone more experienced can read it and make it work better and use it for their campaign. Just from looking at requiem a lot of the bloodlines look way weak, or way too strong for the exp investment anyway. Either way, its fun to make them, and if I make them I might as well put them out there so someone can see them. I didn't bother to rebalance the Graveworm merit because i'm just tired fiddling with it, still its there no need to delete it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 08-21-2016, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}